        <type>bool</type>
        <definition>template bool csmp::SKUA_Interface::ImportElementPropertyValuesFromSKUA</definition>
        <argsstring>(Model&lt; dim &gt; &amp;, const std::string &amp;data_file=std::string())</argsstring>
        <name>ImportElementPropertyValuesFromSKUA</name>
        <qualifiedname>csmp::SKUA_Interface::ImportElementPropertyValuesFromSKUA</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_model" kindref="compound">Model</ref>&lt; dim &gt; &amp;</type>
          <defname>model</defname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const std::string &amp;</type>
          <declname>data_file</declname>
          <defval>std::string()</defval>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>region-by-region property assignment from column-based texfile (Kuncho Kurtev) </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Using the supplied region names and &quot;element number&quot; values, maps the data from the input file onto the current model. The input file is expected to be named after the current model with the extension &quot;-element_barycentres.txt&quot;. Its expected format is:</para>
<para>header line axes titles: region-name(string), region-id(number 0..n-1), element-id(number 0..n-1), - comma-separated list of property names comma-seperated data... EOF</para>
<para><simplesect kind="attention"><para>properties are mapped region by region so that values do not spill across region boundaries; not found non-NON-DATA values are reported</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="attention"><para>property values are mapped only if they are within range; out-of range values are reported, but ignored.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="attention"><para>if a region does not exist, an error is reported</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="attention"><para>property values will only be written to elements whose property flag is not DIRICH or fixed</para>
</simplesect>
<xrefsect id="todo_1_todo000125"><xreftitle>Todo</xreftitle><xrefdescription><para>TODO: expand to handle tensor properties as well</para>
</xrefdescription></xrefsect></para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>SKM </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
