        <name>ConvertRockTypesIntoRegions</name>
        <qualifiedname>csmp::SKUA_Interface::ConvertRockTypesIntoRegions</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_model" kindref="compound">Model</ref>&lt; 3U &gt; &amp;</type>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const std::string &amp;</type>
          <declname>rocktype_info_file</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>For each rock type the elements will be converted into regions with the corresponding name. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Reads file with the mapping from integer codes to region names and creates corresponding model regions. Elements with rocktype identifiers that are not contained in the regions file are ignore, but the unrecognised codes are reported to screen and file. The file has the following format:</para>
<para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">headline<sp/>(printed<sp/>to<sp/>screen)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">identifier<sp/>value<sp/><sp/>tab<sp/><sp/>region<sp/>name<sp/>(can<sp/>contain<sp/>white<sp/>space)</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><simplesect kind="attention"><para>if the rocktype file info file is omitted, the function will search for a file called: &quot;model_name-rocktype-identifiers.txt&quot;</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>only the first 2 tokens in each line of the file are read, allowing the user to add comments afterwards</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="author"><para>SKM </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>22/8/2018 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
